    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "为什么「神经语言模型」会成为人工智能史上值得单独记住的一步？",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "神经概率语言模型用学习得到的分布式词表示和神经预测器取代稀疏的 n-gram 表。在 word2vec 和 Transformer 语言模型之前，它把语言建模与表示学习连接起来。",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-neural-probabilistic-language-model"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "词被映射为向量，与上下文组合后用于预测下一个词。",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-neural-probabilistic-language-model"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "专家通常把神经概率语言模型视为从稀疏 n-gram 方法走向学习型分布式表示的重要桥梁。它的长期影响在于证明语言预测可以学习可复用的词向量和上下文表示。",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-neural-probabilistic-language-model"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "当今天的系统规模越来越大时，「神经语言模型」留下的思路还有哪些价值，又有哪些边界值得重新追问？",
